! HIBO LAB B JULY SINGLE-SETPOINT EXCITATION - 2026-10-21
! July weather-run days: ThermostatSetpoint:SingleHeatingOrCooling (type 3).
! The actual common heating/cooling target is 20,22,24,26,28 C.
! No +/-0.5 C offsets are applied during the July weather run.
! Every original July switch time and central-reference value is preserved.
! Target values equal (original heating setpoint + cooling setpoint)/2.
! The fixed mixed-level schedule is retained; it is not newly optimized.
! Other zones, HVAC equipment, sizing inputs, weather settings and existing
! output requests are unchanged. Shared AHU/interzone coupling remains active.
! Lab B retains its original dual controls outside July and on design days.
! Run period: July 1-31, July 1 Sunday, one-minute timestep, DST disabled.
! Calibration split remains a downstream choice: July 1 conditioning,
! July 2-22 training, July 23-31 validation; no MCMC is run by this IDF.
! Additional timestep outputs expose the applied single setpoint and mode.

!-Generator IDFEditor 1.53
!-Option SortedOrder

!-NOTE: All comments with '!-' are ignored by the IDFEditor and are generated automatically.
!-      Use '!' comments if they need to be retained when using the IDFEditor.


!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: VERSION ===========

! HIBO TASK 1 - REFERENCED MATERIALS REVISION - 2026-09-25
! Parent: HIBO_Task1_Standard_Ground(1).idf (EnergyPlus22.2).
! Published material/reference-assembly values are identified beside each field.
! Generic references and calculated equivalents do not certify installed products.
! Geometry, HVAC, controls, gains, run periods, outputs and ground temperatures
! retain their original active values. APC-1 material is renamed to identify
! the selected Armstrong ULTIMA High NRC1940 reference, consistently in all uses.
! Floors use the existing Ground boundary and explicit fill/slab/finish layers.
! Annual results are regenerated with EnergyPlus22.2 and Omaha725500 TMY3.
Version,
    22.2;                    !- Version Identifier


!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: SIMULATIONCONTROL ===========

SimulationControl,
    Yes,                     !- Do Zone Sizing Calculation
    Yes,                     !- Do System Sizing Calculation
    No,                      !- Do Plant Sizing Calculation
    No,                      !- Run Simulation for Sizing Periods
    Yes,                     !- Run Simulation for Weather File Run Periods
    No,                      !- Do HVAC Sizing Simulation for Sizing Periods
    3;                       !- Maximum Number of HVAC Sizing Simulation Passes


!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: BUILDING ===========

Building,
    Building 1,              !- Name
    333,                     !- North Axis {deg}
    Suburbs,                 !- Terrain
    0.04,                    !- Loads Convergence Tolerance Value {W}
    0.4,                     !- Temperature Convergence Tolerance Value {deltaC}
    FullExterior,            !- Solar Distribution
    25,                      !- Maximum Number of Warmup Days
    6;                       !- Minimum Number of Warmup Days


!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: SHADOWCALCULATION ===========

ShadowCalculation,
    PolygonClipping,         !- Shading Calculation Method
    Periodic,                !- Shading Calculation Update Frequency Method
    20,                      !- Shading Calculation Update Frequency
    15000,                   !- Maximum Figures in Shadow Overlap Calculations
    SutherlandHodgman,       !- Polygon Clipping Algorithm
    512,                     !- Pixel Counting Resolution
    SimpleSkyDiffuseModeling,!- Sky Diffuse Modeling Algorithm
    No,                      !- Output External Shading Calculation Results
    No,                      !- Disable Self-Shading Within Shading Zone Groups
    No;                      !- Disable Self-Shading From Shading Zone Groups to Other Zones


!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: SURFACECONVECTIONALGORITHM:INSIDE ===========

